³1version³21³2ts³21097884656³2ip³2217.247.138.98³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3*³3text³3= Definition of L'User =

This term generally comes from the computer community. It is pseudo-French for "The User", but meant to equate users with losers. It is the result mainly of system operator's exasperation at the trouble the users could get themselves into, many times the result of not 'undertanding' the system. i.e., that which was generally obvious to the administrator. This relationship repeats itself through most of the technical world whether computer or dishwasher.

But, as there are true Hackers in the world, there are also true L'Users. A true L'Luser understands that there are always other technical areas where even the most brilliant and experienced Hacker becomes a L'User. The only true loser is the one who works at it, or perhaps better, works at nothing.

For here, we L'Users concentrate on the infrastructure of the computer Hacker world, and that mostly means documentation, reviews, and testing but grows out into many other areas. The only requirement is willingness to work and understand and as anywhere maintain standards of conduct.

040127, JunkerIn















